WEBVTT

00:00:02.530 --> 00:00:05.980
Explosions, explosions, la la la!

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:09.480
Explosions, explosions, la la la!

00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:13.190
Explosions, explosions, la la la!

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:14.610
<i>Despite still being a suspect, 
my daily routine with Megumin continued.</i>

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:16.580
Explosion!

00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:21.500
<i>On rainy days...</i>

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:22.930
...losion!

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:26.520
<i>And on snowy days...</i>

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:27.460
...sion!

00:00:30.110 --> 00:00:32.300
<i>Even on peaceful afternoons!</i>

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:33.220
...n!

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:43.260
What do you think of this lovely rainbow?

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:44.520
I give it 120 points!

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:50.320
<i>What am I even doing?</i>

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:52.530
<i>I can't keep this up!</i>

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:07.670
<b>KONOSUBA!
God's Blessing on this Wonderful World! 2</b>

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:25.700
<b>Episode 3   Peace for the Master of This Labyrinth!</b>

00:02:24.230 --> 00:02:25.740
The food is great!

00:02:24.470 --> 00:02:25.740
And this booze is the best!

00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:34.790
Tomorrow we're going to a dungeon.

00:02:34.790 --> 00:02:35.790
No.

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:36.710
We are.

00:02:37.060 --> 00:02:38.430
No, no way!

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:38.430
We are! We are!

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:41.850
I mean, I'm practically 
useless inside a dungeon!

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:43.830
I can't use explosion magic,

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:45.970
which makes me an ordinary civilian!

00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:48.160
Remember when you joined up with us,

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:51.100
and you said you'd carry our bags, 
or whatever we needed?

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:56.400
Hey, can't we wait until Darkness gets back?

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:57.360
Listen to me!

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:59.690
Right now, we've got as much 
debt as some countries!

00:02:59.690 --> 00:03:01.920
If we don't do something, 
we'll starve to death!

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:05.000
Even though I'm being paid more now 
for folding those milk cartons?

00:03:02.030 --> 00:03:03.570
How can you guys not understand this?!

00:03:03.570 --> 00:03:04.220
Stupid!

00:03:04.220 --> 00:03:06.250
Are you stupid?! Of course you are!

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:07.540
Even though I've been selling 
vegetables non-stop?

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:09.200
Those side and part-time jobs

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:11.960
are never going to bring us 
the kind of money we need!

00:03:13.640 --> 00:03:16.140
For beginners... Keele's Dungeon?

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:18.850
Hasn't this place been 
thoroughly explored already?

00:03:18.850 --> 00:03:20.260
Well, the thing is...

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:24.640
Recently, a new passage was
discovered by accident,

00:03:25.110 --> 00:03:29.400
so there was going to be a large-scale 
quest to escort the survey team...

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:32.710
But I asked her to give us the first crack at it.

00:03:32.710 --> 00:03:35.980
That being the case, the other 
adventurers don't know about it yet.

00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:41.360
I see... Then there might still be 
treasure in the unexplored areas.

00:03:42.090 --> 00:03:42.960
Treasure?!

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:45.950
What? Hey, are you guys talking about a score?

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:50.390
It's a very serious matter.

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:52.730
I don't want to drag you into it.

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:55.520
Hey, this expires tonight!

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:57.140
Make good use of it.

00:03:58.140 --> 00:03:59.340
I've got it!

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:05.710
<i>We finally have a chance 
to make some real money.</i>

00:04:05.710 --> 00:04:07.840
<i>We can't afford to have anyone mess it up.</i>

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:10.550
Anyway, there's no telling 
how dangerous it might be,

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:12.350
so watch yourselves out there.

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:13.780
KONOSUBA...

00:04:15.850 --> 00:04:20.360
<b>Exploration Quest</b>

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:20.360
<b>Keele's Dungeon
Investigate the newly discovered route
Difficulty Level: Unknown</b>

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:24.950
For a lowbie dungeon, 
it's annoyingly far from town.

00:04:25.210 --> 00:04:28.360
Being this far from civilization, 
I can blow up whatever I want!

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:30.830
We're going underground, so you'd better not.

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:32.580
Seriously, don't.

00:04:34.130 --> 00:04:39.040
Long, long ago, this dungeon was created 
by the kingdom's greatest arch wizard.

00:04:39.480 --> 00:04:43.780
Why do you suppose he holed 
up in a place like this?

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:45.000
Beats me.

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:49.080
Must be hard to rest in peace when people 
are constantly digging around in your house.

00:04:49.420 --> 00:04:50.010
All right...

00:04:51.260 --> 00:04:54.810
I'll head in first. You guys wait here.

00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:07.620
<i>I've got the thief skills 
"Enemy Detection" and "Lurk."</i>

00:05:08.110 --> 00:05:11.480
<i>By using them, I can avoid enemies 
while I explore the dungeon.</i>

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:14.080
<i>Then there's "Foresight."</i>

00:05:15.350 --> 00:05:20.060
<i>With it, I can navigate through 
dark spaces with ease!</i>

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:27.610
<i>All thanks to one of the few 
advantages of the adventurer class:</i>

00:05:27.610 --> 00:05:30.120
<i>the ability to use skills from other classes.</i>

00:05:30.550 --> 00:05:33.840
<i>It's times like these when you need 
to capitalize on your strengths...</i>

00:05:34.720 --> 00:05:37.930
Hey, hey, are you seriously able to see?

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:40.440
Yes, I am.

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:42.900
Were you listening at all?

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:46.410
You came in here with me, but you 
can't even do anything in the dark.

00:05:47.250 --> 00:05:49.520
Have you forgotten who I am?

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:51.740
This arch priest identity is just an alter-ego.

00:05:52.090 --> 00:05:53.470
Go on, say it.

00:05:53.470 --> 00:05:56.910
Megumin and Darkness might be 
too stubborn to believe it, but...

00:05:56.910 --> 00:05:59.550
Go on, state my real class.

00:05:59.550 --> 00:06:01.050
Debt goddess?

00:06:01.050 --> 00:06:03.250
No! I'm a water goddess, remember?!

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:05.910
In spite of everything, I'm still a goddess!

00:06:05.910 --> 00:06:08.230
I may have lost some of my powers 
down here among mortals,

00:06:08.230 --> 00:06:12.260
but I still have a godlike 
power or two up my sleeve!

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:16.810
I might not be omniscient, but a little 
darkness will be a piece of cake!

00:06:17.490 --> 00:06:20.400
Man, these really are all empty.

00:06:20.890 --> 00:06:23.570
<i>Perhaps she can actually see, but...</i>

00:06:22.850 --> 00:06:23.510
Ow!

00:06:24.120 --> 00:06:26.530
<i>Who knows what trouble 
her bungling will cause?</i>

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:30.460
The thing with dungeons is that 
there are always undead in them.

00:06:30.460 --> 00:06:34.040
And they stalk the living by 
following their life force.

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:38.180
Which means that the Lurk skill isn't 
going to work on undead monsters.

00:06:38.180 --> 00:06:41.660
So I just have to go with you, don't I?

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:43.340
Oh?

00:06:43.580 --> 00:06:48.510
Treasure, treasure, la la la, treasure!

00:06:45.480 --> 00:06:48.090
<i>Seriously, I have an awful feeling about this!</i>

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:52.050
My power...

00:06:52.650 --> 00:06:54.080
My weapon...?

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:55.780
My madness?

00:06:56.750 --> 00:06:59.350
Let my madness manifest!

00:06:59.350 --> 00:07:00.730
Explos—

00:07:04.570 --> 00:07:05.360
This is it...

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:15.670
So this is where the unexplored 
territory starts, huh?

00:07:15.670 --> 00:07:17.720
Maybe it's littered with treasure!

00:07:17.720 --> 00:07:19.660
We're gonna be trouble if it's not.

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:21.620
All right, come on.

00:07:35.910 --> 00:07:38.770
Hey, if my keen eyes aren't deceiving me,

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:42.390
it looks very much like you're 
shaking in fear with each step.

00:07:42.740 --> 00:07:43.800
Well, for the record,

00:07:43.800 --> 00:07:48.650
I can see you pitifully freaking out 
at every little sound we hear, too.

00:07:49.080 --> 00:07:51.760
Even in here, I can still run away,

00:07:51.760 --> 00:07:54.170
so if you detect any monsters, let me know.

00:07:54.170 --> 00:07:57.530
And don't think you can get away with 
touching my butt in the darkness, either.

00:07:58.260 --> 00:08:01.150
Would you like to know what 
I'm thinking about right now?

00:08:01.530 --> 00:08:03.730
I'm considering how plausible it would be

00:08:03.730 --> 00:08:06.750
to ditch you down here in 
the depths of the dungeon.

00:08:09.980 --> 00:08:14.030
Oh, Kazuma, you're such a joker! Tee-hee!

00:08:14.030 --> 00:08:15.710
Aqua, you dummy.

00:08:15.710 --> 00:08:20.490
Haven't you known me long enough by 
now to know I'm not playing around?

00:08:24.890 --> 00:08:26.230
Something's coming.

00:08:26.230 --> 00:08:28.110
My Enemy Detection is picking it up.

00:08:28.710 --> 00:08:29.630
Shh.

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:32.550
What? What is that?

00:08:32.550 --> 00:08:34.460
Are you showing me shadow puppets?

00:08:34.460 --> 00:08:36.410
Okay, put a light on!

00:08:36.410 --> 00:08:38.910
Forget your silly little 
fox and rabbit shadows.

00:08:38.910 --> 00:08:41.390
I'll show you a perfect 
mobile fortress Destroyer!

00:08:41.390 --> 00:08:42.450
That's not it!

00:08:42.450 --> 00:08:45.120
That gesture meant "an enemy 
is coming, so let's run away!"

00:08:55.690 --> 00:08:57.690
What the hell was that?

00:08:57.690 --> 00:09:01.280
I could see its shape with Foresight, 
but not what it actually was...

00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:05.090
That's a low-level demon called a gremlin.

00:09:05.090 --> 00:09:08.040
You sometimes get weak demons 
in dungeons like these.

00:09:09.300 --> 00:09:13.110
Wait, so you can actually see 
pretty well in this darkness?

00:09:13.110 --> 00:09:15.150
As well as I can in daylight.

00:09:15.430 --> 00:09:18.020
You said before that you'd 
heard me rustling around

00:09:18.020 --> 00:09:19.870
when we were sleeping in the stables...

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:21.550
I didn't see what.

00:09:21.550 --> 00:09:24.540
Once I heard you rustling around, 
I turned the other way to try and sleep.

00:09:26.670 --> 00:09:28.910
Thank you for that, Aqua-sama.

00:09:48.300 --> 00:09:50.610
Oh, it's just some adventurer's corpse.

00:09:50.980 --> 00:09:53.360
So someone else has made it this far before?

00:09:54.950 --> 00:09:56.630
I wonder what's up ahead.

00:09:57.370 --> 00:09:59.440
Kazuma, wait a second.

00:10:00.820 --> 00:10:04.120
Oh, lost soul who died with 
unfulfilled ambitions...

00:10:04.650 --> 00:10:07.120
Go, rest in peace.

00:10:12.990 --> 00:10:14.090
That should do it.

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:16.950
Aqua, something's up with you today...

00:10:16.950 --> 00:10:19.370
Kazuma, I can't believe you went, "Phwah!"

00:10:19.370 --> 00:10:22.470
After playing tough and coming in 
here alone, you're like, "Phwah!"

00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:26.550
<i>Maybe I really should ditch her.</i>

00:10:34.910 --> 00:10:37.410
Burst forth! Explosion!

00:10:42.550 --> 00:10:45.320
<i>Normally, this kind of thing 
involves watching for traps,</i>

00:10:45.320 --> 00:10:47.610
<i>keeping your eyes peeled for monsters,</i>

00:10:47.610 --> 00:10:52.040
<i>and mapping each room, one by one, 
while carefully proceeding.</i>

00:10:52.040 --> 00:10:54.960
<i>What we're doing probably 
seems like heresy to people</i>

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:56.510
<i>who take dungeon crawling seriously.</i>

00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:00.980
Nothing good...

00:11:00.980 --> 00:11:02.700
Hey, Kazuma.

00:11:02.200 --> 00:11:03.130
Yes, Kazuma here.

00:11:02.700 --> 00:11:06.700
When you put it that way, 
you make me feel like a burglar.

00:11:06.700 --> 00:11:07.970
Don't say that.

00:11:07.970 --> 00:11:10.350
I'm feeling kind of guilty about that myself.

00:11:12.270 --> 00:11:13.960
Hey, treasure! There's treasure!

00:11:13.960 --> 00:11:16.390
A treasure chest! We did it!

00:11:16.390 --> 00:11:17.760
Hey, slow down!

00:11:17.760 --> 00:11:19.640
Obvious treasure chests like that tend to be...

00:11:22.980 --> 00:11:25.990
Yeah, my Enemy Detection skill is going off.

00:11:39.260 --> 00:11:40.510
D-Disgusting!

00:11:40.930 --> 00:11:45.710
I remember the Guild people saying 
to be careful of Dungeon Mimics...

00:11:45.710 --> 00:11:46.780
Some of them even

00:11:46.780 --> 00:11:50.060
pretend to be humans in order 
to prey on other monsters.

00:11:50.060 --> 00:11:52.140
Monsters, too?! Talk about nasty!

00:11:52.710 --> 00:11:56.620
<i>The struggle of natural selection 
even shows up in dungeons...</i>

00:11:57.430 --> 00:12:00.250
<i>This world really is a rough place.</i>

00:12:01.310 --> 00:12:02.870
S-Stop that!

00:12:02.870 --> 00:12:04.150
Don't! You can't!

00:12:04.150 --> 00:12:06.560
Trying to put me into something so shameful...

00:12:06.560 --> 00:12:07.490
Curse you!

00:12:08.030 --> 00:12:10.470
I'll kill you!

00:12:12.720 --> 00:12:14.000
Turn Undead!

00:12:18.740 --> 00:12:22.750
Souls that wander this dark, cold dungeon.

00:12:23.150 --> 00:12:25.010
You may rest in peace now.

00:12:25.220 --> 00:12:27.430
<i>Something's different about Aqua today!</i>

00:12:27.430 --> 00:12:30.600
<i>She looks like a goddess you could take 
out in public and not be ashamed of!</i>

00:12:32.320 --> 00:12:32.910
Master!

00:12:32.910 --> 00:12:34.400
Turn Undead!

00:12:34.740 --> 00:12:35.410
Master!

00:12:35.410 --> 00:12:36.740
Turn Undead!

00:12:37.590 --> 00:12:38.590
Master!

00:12:38.590 --> 00:12:43.080
Turn Undead! Turn Undead! Turn Undead! 
Turn Undead! Turn Undead!

00:12:43.080 --> 00:12:44.110
Nature's Beauty!

00:12:44.430 --> 00:12:47.870
God Blow!

00:12:55.340 --> 00:12:56.820
Man, you've been a huge help.

00:12:56.820 --> 00:12:59.390
I really would've been in 
trouble if I'd been alone.

00:12:59.390 --> 00:13:02.880
Oh? Finally realizing how great I am?

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:05.050
You can praise me even more, if you want.

00:13:05.610 --> 00:13:07.850
But doesn't this seem weird to you?

00:13:08.040 --> 00:13:09.120
What do you mean?

00:13:09.120 --> 00:13:11.570
There are so many undead around.

00:13:11.570 --> 00:13:15.140
No party could've made it through 
here without an arch priest...

00:13:15.140 --> 00:13:16.030
Wait.

00:13:16.030 --> 00:13:18.860
I can still smell undead in the area.

00:13:18.860 --> 00:13:20.960
Sniff, sniff... Sniff, sniff... Sniff, sniff....

00:13:20.960 --> 00:13:22.110
Sniff, sniff... Sniff, sniff...

00:13:22.630 --> 00:13:24.290
Sniff, sniff, sniff....

00:13:24.290 --> 00:13:25.610
Sniff, sniff, sniff....

00:13:24.290 --> 00:13:25.610
I don't see anything.

00:13:25.820 --> 00:13:29.020
That's weird. I definitely smell something.

00:13:32.560 --> 00:13:34.210
Hey, are you okay?

00:13:34.210 --> 00:13:37.290
Is there a priest among you?

00:13:41.410 --> 00:13:47.630
My name is Keele. I built this dungeon 
and kidnapped a noble's daughter.

00:13:49.070 --> 00:13:51.870
I am an evil wizard.

00:13:55.190 --> 00:13:57.700
Great wizard Keele.

00:13:57.700 --> 00:14:00.470
For your contributions to this kingdom,

00:14:00.470 --> 00:14:03.330
you will be granted one wish.

00:14:05.000 --> 00:14:07.490
I have but one wish...

00:14:08.280 --> 00:14:13.220
For my beloved to no longer 
suffer, but to be happy.

00:14:14.310 --> 00:14:15.250
You wretch!

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:19.930
She was married off for 
political reasons, you see.

00:14:19.930 --> 00:14:22.290
But the king showed her no love,

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:24.630
and she was treated poorly within the palace.

00:14:25.330 --> 00:14:26.690
That being the case...

00:14:26.690 --> 00:14:30.010
If he had no use for her, 
why not let me take her away?

00:14:31.420 --> 00:14:35.180
So I says that to him and run off with her!

00:14:36.160 --> 00:14:40.420
In other words, you're not an 
evil wizard, but a good one?

00:14:40.420 --> 00:14:42.350
Rather, I <i>was</i> one!

00:14:42.350 --> 00:14:47.360
And when I proposed, 
she immediately accepted!

00:14:47.780 --> 00:14:52.960
While we were eloping, I found myself 
facing off against the whole kingdom!

00:14:53.370 --> 00:14:55.900
Oh, those were glorious days.

00:14:56.370 --> 00:15:00.670
By the way, that's her right over there.

00:15:00.950 --> 00:15:04.170
Well? Doesn't she have the 
most beautiful clavicle?

00:15:05.120 --> 00:15:06.780
I'm not sure what to say.

00:15:05.490 --> 00:15:08.080
Beautiful! Beautiful! Beautiful!

00:15:06.780 --> 00:15:09.760
She managed to pass on in peace.

00:15:09.760 --> 00:15:12.200
That being the case, 
I've a favor to ask of you.

00:15:12.200 --> 00:15:12.930
A favor?

00:15:13.260 --> 00:15:14.040
Yes.

00:15:14.610 --> 00:15:17.550
Would you purify me?

00:15:18.280 --> 00:15:22.440
The young lady is a priest with 
enough power to do so, correct?

00:15:28.910 --> 00:15:32.520
<i>It seems that Keele was gravely 
injured while protecting his lady,</i>

00:15:32.520 --> 00:15:34.270
<i>and in order to keep her safe,</i>

00:15:34.270 --> 00:15:37.110
<i>he abandoned his humanity and became a lich.</i>

00:15:38.090 --> 00:15:42.040
<i>And in spite of myself, I thought 
that this lich was a pretty cool guy.</i>

00:15:43.800 --> 00:15:45.900
Okay, everything's ready.

00:15:45.900 --> 00:15:47.470
I'm really grateful.

00:15:47.470 --> 00:15:51.090
Unfortunately, undead can't do anything 
as surreal as killing themselves.

00:15:51.420 --> 00:15:55.850
While I was waiting to slowly decay,
I sensed a tremendous holy power

00:15:55.850 --> 00:15:59.390
and was snapped out of my long slumber!

00:16:04.810 --> 00:16:09.610
Arch Wizard Keele, who forsook god's 
law and willingly became a lich...

00:16:10.150 --> 00:16:14.110
In the name of the goddess of water, 
Aqua, your sin is forgiven.

00:16:14.880 --> 00:16:16.550
<i>Who in the world is this?</i>

00:16:17.860 --> 00:16:20.720
When you awaken, you will 
likely meet a goddess

00:16:20.720 --> 00:16:23.120
with unnaturally large breasts, named Eris.

00:16:23.560 --> 00:16:25.640
If a difference in age doesn't matter to you,

00:16:25.640 --> 00:16:27.500
or the trappings of man and woman,

00:16:27.500 --> 00:16:29.720
and you'll accept whatever form it may take...

00:16:30.180 --> 00:16:34.130
Then ask for her help in 
meeting your beloved again.

00:16:34.590 --> 00:16:37.720
I'm sure she'll make your wish come true.

00:16:38.380 --> 00:16:40.140
Thank you so much.

00:16:43.900 --> 00:16:46.150
Sacred Turn Undead.

00:16:54.670 --> 00:16:57.500
<i>Dear wife, I'm coming soon.</i>

00:17:06.690 --> 00:17:07.580
Let's head back.

00:17:12.590 --> 00:17:17.000
<i>With the treasure Keele gave us, 
we left the chamber.</i>

00:17:18.070 --> 00:17:19.040
Hey, Aqua.

00:17:19.040 --> 00:17:19.900
What's up?

00:17:19.900 --> 00:17:24.960
That guy said he woke up because 
he sensed a tremendous holy power.

00:17:24.960 --> 00:17:25.690
Yep.

00:17:25.870 --> 00:17:29.160
We didn't run into all 
those undead back there

00:17:29.160 --> 00:17:31.700
because of you, did we?

00:17:34.860 --> 00:17:40.590
I-I-I don't... think that's... the case...

00:17:42.940 --> 00:17:45.970
That reminds me, when the dullahan attacked,

00:17:45.970 --> 00:17:48.990
didn't his undead minions go after you?

00:17:48.990 --> 00:17:50.830
H-Hey, Kazuma...

00:17:50.830 --> 00:17:52.710
Why are you moving so far away?

00:17:52.980 --> 00:17:58.010
Shouldn't we stick together 
in case a monster attacks?

00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:03.810
If you're trying to ditch me down here,

00:18:03.810 --> 00:18:05.590
that's not gonna happen!

00:18:04.190 --> 00:18:05.590
Hey, let go!

00:18:05.590 --> 00:18:07.520
You can't make it back on your own

00:18:07.520 --> 00:18:09.450
without me to fight off the undead!

00:18:09.450 --> 00:18:11.270
Please don't leave me behind!

00:18:11.270 --> 00:18:14.030
Then you really did draw those undead to us?!

00:18:14.330 --> 00:18:16.870
You can't leave me! 
There're other monsters down here, too!

00:18:16.870 --> 00:18:18.720
Don't leave me alone!

00:18:25.430 --> 00:18:26.520
Lurk...

00:18:26.810 --> 00:18:27.500
Wait!

00:18:27.790 --> 00:18:29.110
Hang on, Kazuma!

00:18:29.110 --> 00:18:31.240
Why are you only using Lurk on yourself?!

00:18:31.240 --> 00:18:33.690
You wouldn't really... Cut the cruel jokes!

00:18:33.690 --> 00:18:36.570
I'm sorry, I'm so sorry! 
I shouldn't have done it!

00:18:36.570 --> 00:18:39.320
I'm sorry, so use Lurk on me, too!

00:18:39.320 --> 00:18:40.780
I'm sorry, Kazuma!

00:18:40.780 --> 00:18:42.260
Please, Kazuma-sama!

00:18:45.200 --> 00:18:47.020
KONOSUBA!

00:18:48.390 --> 00:18:50.690
May I ask what happened?

00:18:52.250 --> 00:18:53.380
It was Kazuma!

00:18:53.220 --> 00:18:58.410
Don't blame me! It's your fault 
for being catnip to undead!

00:18:53.380 --> 00:18:54.870
Kazuma, he...

00:18:58.410 --> 00:18:59.460
It's not my fault!

00:18:59.460 --> 00:19:04.450
I was born divine and overflowing 
with vital energy!

00:19:04.670 --> 00:19:05.880
Or what are you saying?

00:19:05.880 --> 00:19:10.350
Am I supposed to lower my holy aura 
to that of Kazuma, the shut-in NEET?!

00:19:10.350 --> 00:19:13.430
Think about how sad all the 
devout Axis cult members

00:19:13.430 --> 00:19:15.590
scattered throughout the world would feel!

00:19:15.950 --> 00:19:18.650
She doesn't even feel a bit guilty!

00:19:18.650 --> 00:19:22.590
You could learn a lesson about 
spiritual purity from those two!

00:19:22.590 --> 00:19:26.140
A shut-in NEET is telling a goddess 
to take cues from a pair of undead?!

00:19:26.140 --> 00:19:29.600
<b>Keele's Dungeon
Exploration Complete
Special Bonus: Keele's Treasure</b>

00:19:27.060 --> 00:19:29.600
<b>Today's Results</b>

00:19:33.070 --> 00:19:34.730
Cheers!

00:19:35.880 --> 00:19:38.770
This proves chances are worth taking, 
even if they seem unlikely!

00:19:38.770 --> 00:19:41.530
And thanks to me, it was a huge success!

00:19:41.530 --> 00:19:43.290
We can divide up the spoils 9:1.

00:19:43.290 --> 00:19:45.780
Idiot! All of this is going toward our debt!

00:19:46.190 --> 00:19:48.720
But we can at least order refills today, right?

00:19:48.720 --> 00:19:51.830
Excuse me! Keep the drinks coming!

00:19:51.830 --> 00:19:56.270
All I did was wait at the entrance, 
so it doesn't feel like I deserve it,

00:19:56.270 --> 00:19:57.190
but thanks for—

00:19:56.840 --> 00:19:58.340
You're too young for that!

00:19:59.040 --> 00:20:00.250
That's no fair!

00:20:00.250 --> 00:20:03.580
Please let me drink some! Come on!

00:20:03.580 --> 00:20:05.470
A little bit couldn't hurt!

00:20:03.850 --> 00:20:04.770
Nope!

00:20:05.470 --> 00:20:08.970
I can't handle these part-time 
jobs anymore! We gotta do quests!

00:20:09.290 --> 00:20:11.510
Hup! Nature's Beauty!

00:20:11.510 --> 00:20:12.480
There it is!

00:20:14.200 --> 00:20:18.050
Miss, you really did us 
a huge favor this time.

00:20:18.050 --> 00:20:21.320
This is on me. Please enjoy.

00:20:21.670 --> 00:20:22.720
Uh, thanks...

00:20:22.720 --> 00:20:24.010
You're paying?!

00:20:24.010 --> 00:20:24.950
Seriously?!

00:20:24.950 --> 00:20:28.520
Hey, guys! Drinks are on Kazuma tonight!

00:20:29.660 --> 00:20:32.350
You can bet on Kazuma! He always 
comes through when it counts!

00:20:32.350 --> 00:20:33.670
That's Kazuma-san for you!

00:20:33.830 --> 00:20:36.960
Kazuma! Kazuma! Kazuma!

00:20:36.960 --> 00:20:40.170
Kazuma! Kazuma! Kazuma!

00:20:38.400 --> 00:20:40.960
All right! Everybody drink up!

00:20:41.480 --> 00:20:43.470
Hey, Kazuma! Do that thing!

00:20:43.830 --> 00:20:47.220
Well, since you asked!

00:20:50.720 --> 00:20:54.780
Steal! Steal! Steal!

00:20:54.780 --> 00:20:57.230
Steal!

00:20:57.660 --> 00:20:59.340
Kazuma's paying for drinks?

00:21:05.050 --> 00:21:07.080
No!

00:21:07.080 --> 00:21:09.410
Give me back my panties!

00:21:12.410 --> 00:21:14.590
Steal! Steal!

00:21:14.420 --> 00:21:15.590
Stop it!

00:21:14.590 --> 00:21:18.250
I can use Steal, too! Steal! Steal!

00:21:20.160 --> 00:21:21.560
Good grief...

00:21:22.270 --> 00:21:23.610
M-Megumin!

00:21:24.310 --> 00:21:26.310
Wh-What a coincidence, running into you here!

00:21:26.310 --> 00:21:27.870
How lucky!

00:21:27.870 --> 00:21:29.470
Today we'll duel with these!

00:21:32.030 --> 00:21:34.190
Very well! Challenge accepted!

00:21:33.520 --> 00:21:36.110
Garter belt!

00:21:37.210 --> 00:21:41.230
Give them back!

00:21:37.770 --> 00:21:41.230
<i>This doesn't pay my debt, and I'm 
still under suspicion, but...</i>

00:21:41.790 --> 00:21:43.230
<i>It's kinda fun!</i>

00:21:43.230 --> 00:21:45.570
<i>I actually feel like an adventurer!</i>

00:21:46.770 --> 00:21:49.140
We're gonna drink 'til morning, people!

00:21:49.140 --> 00:21:51.770
Yeah!

00:21:56.840 --> 00:21:58.230
<i>What am I even doing?</i>

00:21:58.930 --> 00:22:00.590
<i>I can't keep this up!</i>

00:23:31.010 --> 00:23:41.260
<b>Roar, storms! Echo, thunder! Shake this world, and all be blown away!
With one blast, no enemies remain. Flowers bloom, butterflies dance,
Grandpa's rheumatoid arthritis is cured, the dead rise, and you shed tears of joy.
Now, to share with your family, enjoy the wonder of explosion magic! Remember to
follow the rules. Try and avoid using it in the vicinity of people and their homes.
Remember to use it in a safe environment. Always have parental supervision.
Limit use to one per day. All in the name of effective explosion magic use.</b>

